In article <18219@helios.TAMU.EDU> z0w3116@venus.tamu.edu writes:
>You are stridently aligned.		<-- Q: What does this mean?
SPOILERS AHEAD
This means that you have killed the right monsters. Normally one is always
stridently aligned (except at the very beginning of the game). It has
something to do with how your god reacts on your prayer. If you are not
stridently aligned your praying won't do annything good.
Offering humans and unicorns of your own alignment will seriously decrease
your alignement.
stridently if the alignment counter is > 3
haltingly                              > 0 and <= 3
normaly                                = 0
strayed                                < 0

>You have extra luck.			<-- Luckstone??
Correct, and it is not cursed, otherwise you'll have had reduced luck.
In fact it is the sum of all the luckstones you are carrying.
Let me just assume it is one luck stone.

>Bad luck does not time out for you.	<-- Q: What do these mean?
Your luck stone is cursed or uncursed.
>Good luck does not time out for you.	<-- 
Your luck stone is blessed or uncursed.

Combining the above two: you have an uncursed luck stone.

Luck can be in the range of [-10,10] (may vary a bit on full moon).
Normally it goes back to 0 (just like the hitpoint/energie recuperates).
If however you have a cursed luckstone, this recuperating will not be
done if your luck is negative. This is a serious problem, as negative luck
is very bad (influence your hit change to a monster etc). Good luck (i.e.
positive) will still be decreasing towards 0.
If you have a blessed luck stone, only the negative luck will increase to 0,
while positive luck is not decreased anymore. This is what you want to have.

>Two more questions: 
>Seems shops never appear at deep levels, is it supposed so?
Your 'seems' is correct. There is a small change that a shop is ona deep
level. The latest level a shop is generated is the medusa level minus 1
(i.e. the level before the medusa). Also on level 1 there is never a shop.
The change that a level has a shop is: 3 / level.
This looks like that on levels 2 and 3 there must be always a shop, but
there is the restriction that a shopkeeper doesn't like all rooms to start
his business in: like a room with a backdoor or stairs or unlit etc. If no
such room is available on the level then there will be no shop.

>What's the use of gems besides selling them for money?
When leaving the dungeon at the end, you'll get some bonus points.
Also throwing gems at unicorns (best of your own alignment) will increase
your luck:
unidentified gems: always +1 (even if the gem is worthless),
piece of glass   : no harm is done,
jewel            : +5 to unicorn of own alignment, [-3,3] to other unicorn.

